{"subject": "📊 Daily Portfolio: GOOG -8.1% (Sep29 IBKR, feed blocked) | portfolio.json stale — SPXC appears already exited", "html_body": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n</head>\n<body style=\"margin: 0; padding: 0; background-color: #f4f5f7; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; color: #111827;\">\n\n<table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" border=\"0\" width=\"100%\" style=\"background-color: #f4f5f7; padding: 24px 12px;\">\n  <tr>\n    <td align=\"center\">\n      <table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" border=\"0\" width=\"600\" style=\"max-width: 600px; background-color: #ffffff; border-radius: 12px; overflow: hidden;\">\n\n        <!-- DECISIONS NEEDED -->\n        <tr>\n          <td style=\"padding: 16px 20px; background-color: #fef3c7; border-bottom: 1px solid #fde68a;\">\n            <p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; color: #92400e; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px;\">⚠️ Decisions needed — portfolio.json is stale, SPXC looks already closed</p>\n            <p style=\"margin: 6px 0 0 0; font-size: 13px; color: #78350f; line-height: 1.6;\">\n              portfolio.json (last_updated 2026-08-25) still lists SPXC as an open position with $330.60 cash. But the <strong>Sept 29 stock-finder run pulled live IBKR data</strong> and found: only GOOG open, cash $432.16, net liq $533.80 — SPXC is gone. The cash delta ($432.16 − $330.60 = $101.56) lines up almost exactly with the $205.00 GTC exit-limit (0.5 sh × $205 = $102.50 gross, minus ~$1 commission), not the $186.90 stop (~$92.45 net) — so SPXC most likely exited near its small-profit target, not the stop. <strong>This is inference, not a confirmed fill.</strong> Action: pull the SPXC trade confirmation from IBKR (price/date/P&amp;L) and run <code>portfolio-manager</code> to sync the file — it's been carrying a false \"open position\" and a stale cash balance for over a month.\n            </p>\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n\n        <!-- HERO BANNER -->\n        <tr>\n          <td style=\"background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1e293b 0%, #334155 100%); padding: 32px 24px; color: #ffffff;\">\n            <p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: 1px; text-transform: uppercase; color: #94a3b8;\">Daily Portfolio Check</p>\n            <p style=\"margin: 4px 0 16px 0; font-size: 14px; color: #cbd5e1;\">Thursday, October 1, 2026 — Kuwait time</p>\n\n            <table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\n              <tr>\n                <td>\n                  <p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 11px; color: #94a3b8; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px;\">GOOG unrealized P&amp;L (last reconciled, Sept 29)</p>\n                  <p style=\"margin: 4px 0 0 0; font-size: 30px; font-weight: 700; color: #ef4444;\">-$8.96 <span style=\"font-size: 16px; opacity: 0.8;\">(-8.1%)</span></p>\n                  <p style=\"margin: 2px 0 0 0; font-size: 11px; color: #94a3b8;\">Today's own price fetch (Yahoo + stooq) failed again — 22nd straight EGRESS_BLOCKED day. Figure above is 2 days old, sourced from stock-finder's live IBKR pull, not today's quote.</p>\n                </td>\n              </tr>\n            </table>\n\n            <table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"margin-top: 16px; padding-top: 16px; border-top: 1px solid #475569;\">\n              <tr>\n                <td style=\"font-size: 13px; color: #e2e8f0;\">\n                  🎯 <strong>Investment goal:</strong> ~$533.80 / $1,000 (Sept 29 net liq) — <strong>~$466.20 to go</strong> (~53% there). Target date (Jul 31) already passed; still awaiting a reset.\n                </td>\n              </tr>\n            </table>\n\n            <p style=\"margin: 16px 0 0 0; padding-top: 16px; border-top: 1px solid #475569; font-size: 13px; color: #e2e8f0;\">Price feed down 22 straight days. Bigger story: SPXC's month-overdue defense-rule exit appears to have already happened — portfolio.json just never caught up.</p>\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n\n        <!-- MACRO CONTEXT -->\n        <tr>\n          <td style=\"padding: 16px 24px; background-color: #0d0d0d; border-left: 3px solid #f59e0b;\">\n            <p style=\"margin: 0 0 8px 0; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; color: #f59e0b; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px;\">🌍 Macro Context — Oct 1, 2026</p>\n            <p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 13px; color: #e5e7eb; line-height: 1.8; font-family: monospace;\">\n              Buffett Indicator: &nbsp;234.4% &nbsp;<span style=\"background-color: #b91c1c; color: #fff; padding: 2px 8px; border-radius: 10px; font-size: 11px;\">🔴 ALL-TIME EXTREME</span><br>\n              S&amp;P Forward P/E: &nbsp;~19.3x &nbsp;(vs. avg ~16-18x)<br>\n              Trend: &nbsp;→ roughly flat vs June's 232.5% reading\n            </p>\n            <p style=\"margin: 10px 0 0 0; font-size: 12px; color: #d1d5db; line-height: 1.6;\">Market cap is still ~2.3x the entire US economy — every reading this high has historically preceded a multi-year bear market. One widely-cited source (gurufocus, Sept 2026) puts it at 234.4%; a differently-calculated \"live\" feed showed 298.7% the same week — methodology, not just the market, moves this number (see Buffett Indicator Part 3 in your education track).</p>\n            <p style=\"margin: 8px 0 0 0; font-size: 12px; color: #d1d5db; line-height: 1.6;\">Implication: no reason to change course on GOOG, but with ~80% of the account now in cash (pending reconciliation), don't force fresh exposure into this macro backdrop without a real catalyst — let stock-finder earn the entry.</p>\n            <p style=\"margin: 8px 0 0 0; font-size: 11px; color: #9ca3af;\"><em>Last historical episodes at this level: 2000 dot-com peak, 2021 COVID bubble peak.</em></p>\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n\n        <!-- POSITION NEWS -->\n        <tr>\n          <td style=\"padding: 20px 24px 0 24px;\">\n            <p style=\"margin: 0 0 12px 0; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 600;\">📰 Position News — Oct 1, 2026</p>\n            <p style=\"margin: 0 0 10px 0; font-size: 13px; color: #374151; line-height: 1.6;\">\n              🔵 <strong>GOOG</strong> — Rebounding off the 50-week SMA; shares reportedly +3.3% on Sept 30 on Gemini crossing 1B+ monthly active users and a $514B AI infrastructure backlog. Headwind: a fresh €403M EU fine adds regulatory friction. Implication: news backdrop supports the thesis holding; still can't confirm today's price vs. the $333.90 stop without a live quote, but nothing here suggests danger.\n            </p>\n            <p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 13px; color: #374151; line-height: 1.6;\">\n              🟢 <strong>SPXC</strong> — No longer held (see Decisions Needed above). For the record: completed the $410M FIS Water bolt-on Sept 15 and was initiated Buy at Vertical Research Sept 28 — both after the halal-driven exit decision, neither relevant now that the position's closed.\n            </p>\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n\n        <!-- POSITION SNAPSHOT TABLE -->\n        <tr>\n          <td style=\"padding: 20px 24px;\">\n            <p style=\"margin: 0 0 4px 0; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 600;\">Position Snapshot</p>\n            <p style=\"margin: 0 0 12px 0; font-size: 12px; color: #9ca3af;\">Prices: Yahoo Finance JSON API (query1 + query2) and stooq all returned EGRESS_BLOCKED today. GOOG figures below are the last reconciled live read (IBKR, via stock-finder, Sept 29) — 2 days old, clearly labeled, not an estimate of today's price. SPXC is carried here only because portfolio.json hasn't been synced yet; treat it as closed pending confirmation.</p>\n\n            <table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadd