e=\"padding: 4px 0;\">Stopped out 8/4 @ $227.91, net −$4.56</td></tr>\n                    <tr><td style=\"padding: 4px 0;\">CELC</td><td style=\"padding: 4px 0;\">Exited 7/15 @ $91.63, net −$26.32 (sell-the-news)</td></tr>\n                    <tr><td style=\"padding: 4px 0;\">CAPR</td><td style=\"padding: 4px 0;\">Stopped out 7/27 @ $5.80, net −$234.73 (gap-through-stop)</td></tr>\n                    <tr><td style=\"padding: 4px 0;\">VRDN</td><td style=\"padding: 4px 0;\">Entry missed (IBKR blocker), event passed</td></tr>\n                    <tr><td style=\"padding: 4px 0;\">VERA</td><td style=\"padding: 4px 0;\">Stopped out 7/17 @ $37.74, net −$33.28</td></tr>\n                  </table>\n                </td>\n              </tr>\n            </table>\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n\n        <!-- CASH DEPLOYMENT -->\n        <tr>\n          <td style=\"padding: 0 24px 20px 24px;\">\n            <table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"background-color: #eff6ff; border: 1px solid #bfdbfe; border-radius: 8px;\">\n              <tr>\n                <td style=\"padding: 16px 20px;\">\n                  <p style=\"margin: 0 0 6px 0; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700; color: #1e40af;\">💵 Cash deployment — ~$432.16 as of Sept 29 (IBKR via stock-finder); portfolio.json's $330.60 is stale</p>\n                  <p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 12px; color: #1e3a8a; line-height: 1.7;\">\n                    Deployable after commission: ~$430 — well above the $30 meaningful-position floor, and now roughly <strong>81% of a ~$534 account</strong> sitting in cash once SPXC's exit is reconciled.<br>\n                    No fresh candidate generated here — that's <code>stock-finder</code>'s job, run on demand. With the price feed down 22 days straight, this is also a good moment to confirm basic account state (exact cash, exact SPXC fill) before putting more to work.<br>\n                    <strong>Your call</strong> — no order plan below since there's no screened candidate to size against real levels (per the no-naked-entry rule).\n                  </p>\n                </td>\n              </tr>\n            </table>\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n\n        <!-- ROTATION -->\n        <tr>\n          <td style=\"padding: 0 24px 20px 24px;\">\n            <p style=\"margin: 0 0 8px 0; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 600;\">🔄 Rotation Suggestions</p>\n            <p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 13px; color: #4b5563; line-height: 1.6;\">None today. GOOG is the only confirmed open position and isn't at a take-profit level. SPXC's apparent exit already freed its cash — once confirmed, run <code>stock-finder</code> for a fresh candidate rather than defaulting to the static large-cap pool, given how much dry powder is now sitting idle.</p>\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n\n        <!-- EDUCATION MODULE -->\n        <tr>\n          <td style=\"padding: 0 24px 24px 24px;\">\n            <table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"background-color: #f1f5f9; border-radius: 8px;\">\n              <tr>\n                <td style=\"padding: 20px 24px;\">\n                  <p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 11px; color: #475569; font-weight: 600; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px;\">📚 Today you learned</p>\n                  <p style=\"margin: 8px 0 0 0; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; color: #0f172a;\">Phase 2 vs. Phase 3 Trial Data — Why the Market Reacts Differently</p>\n                  <p style=\"margin: 12px 0 0 0; font-size: 13px; color: #1e293b; line-height: 1.7;\">\n                    CNTB jumped 124% today on positive Phase 2 COPD data. Phase 2 tests efficacy and dosing in a few hundred patients — it's the first real signal a drug works, so the market reprices hard on a clean readout. But Phase 2-to-approval success rates run under 15% industry-wide; Phase 3 (larger, often 1,000+ patients, powered against the real endpoint) is where most drugs actually die. That's why a Phase 2 pop can fully round-trip on a Phase 3 miss — see your own CELC and VERA exits, both post-approval-stage disappointments. Rule of thumb: size Phase 2 reactions smaller than Phase 3 or PDUFA reactions, since the uncertainty ahead is still larger, not smaller.\n                  </p>\n                  <p style=\"margin: 12px 0 0 0; font-size: 12px; color: #475569; font-style: italic;\">\n                    Also today: <strong>Guidance raise as a standalone catalyst</strong> — IOVA's 30%+ move came purely from raising FY26 revenue guidance above consensus, no new trial data involved; guidance credibility alone can move a stock as much as a beat.\n                  </p>\n                </td>\n              </tr>\n            </table>\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n\n        <!-- FOOTER -->\n        <tr>\n          <td style=\"padding: 16px 24px 24px 24px; border-top: 1px solid #f3f4f6;\">\n            <p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 10px; color: #9ca3af; line-height: 1.5;\">\n              Research output, not financial advice. Past performance does not guarantee future results.\n              Prices: Yahoo Finance JSON API (query1/query2) + stooq — all EGRESS_BLOCKED today, 22nd consecutive day; no price substituted from search results per policy. GOOG figures marked * are a 2-day-old IBKR read relayed via the stock-finder routine's Sept 29 output, not today's quote.\n              portfolio.json last_updated field: 2026-08-25 — stale; recommend a portfolio-manager sync.\n              Generated 2026-10-01, Kuwait time.\n            </p>\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n\n      </table>\n    </td>\n  </tr>\n</table>\n\n</body>\n</html>\n"}